.TH QBT-EXTRACT 1 "2026-11-08" "qbt-extract.sh" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qbt-extract.sh \- extract archives of finished qBittorrent torrents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qbt-extract.sh
[\fB\-n\fR|\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
\fISAVE_PATH\fR \fICONTENT_PATH\fR
[\fINAME\fR]
[\fICATEGORY\fR]
.br
.B qbt-extract.sh
\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qbt-extract.sh
is a thin wrapper meant to be used as qBittorrent's
\(dqRun external program on torrent finished\(dq hook. Configure it with:
.IP
.EX
/home/killian/.local/bin/qbt-extract.sh "%D" "%F" "%N" "%L"
.EE
.P
The arguments are the qBittorrent substitution tokens for the finished
torrent: save path, content path, torrent name and category.
.P
The program filters by category and save path, waits briefly for the
content to settle, locates the archives belonging to the torrent, and
delegates extraction to
.BR extract_archives (1),
which verifies integrity, extracts into a directory named after the archive,
and deletes the archive on success.
.P
All activity is appended to a log file. Concurrent completions are
serialised with
.BR flock (1)
so overlapping torrents cannot process the same archive twice.
.P
qBittorrent fires this hook only after auto-management has moved the
finished torrent out of its incomplete directory, so the content path is
normally already final. The settle wait exists only as a safety net for slow
or unusual moves.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I SAVE_PATH
Final save path of the torrent (qBittorrent token
.BR %D ).
.TP
.I CONTENT_PATH
Content path, i.e. the archive file or the torrent root folder (token
.BR %F ).
If it does not exist, the program falls back to
.IR SAVE_PATH/NAME .
.TP
.I NAME
Torrent name (token
.BR %N ).
Optional; used for the fallback path lookup and for log lines.
.TP
.I CATEGORY
Torrent category (token
.BR %L ).
Optional; an empty value disables the category check but not the path check.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-n\fR, \fB\-\-dry\-run
Log and print what would be extracted without changing anything.
.TP
.B \-h\fR, \fB\-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.SH FILTERS
A torrent is processed only when both checks pass:
.IP \(bu 2
its category equals
.B QBT_EXTRACT_CATEGORY
(default
.IR Image ),
or the category argument is empty; and
.IP \(bu 2
its save path is equal to or below
.B QBT_EXTRACT_PATH
(default
.IR /mnt/shared/img ).
.P
Anything else is skipped with an exit status of 0.
.SH ARCHIVE DISCOVERY
If
.I CONTENT_PATH
is a regular file it is used as the archive. If it is a directory, archives
directly inside it are collected (no recursion). Recognised extensions are
.BR .zip ", " .7z ", " .tar ", " .tar.gz ", " .tgz ", " .tar.bz2 ", " .tbz2 ", "
.BR .tar.xz " and " .txz .
.P
When no archives are found the program exits 0 without logging an error,
which is the normal case for torrents that are not archives.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B QBT_EXTRACT_CATEGORY
Category to process. Default:
.IR Image .
.TP
.B QBT_EXTRACT_PATH
Save path prefix that must contain the torrent. Default:
.IR /mnt/shared/img .
Set to an empty string to disable the path check.
.TP
.B QBT_EXTRACT_EXTRACTOR
Extractor command. Default:
.IR ~/.local/bin/extract_archives.sh .
.TP
.B QBT_EXTRACT_LOG
Log file. Default:
.IR ~/.local/share/qbt-extract.log .
Rotated once to
.IR <log>.1
when it exceeds
.BR QBT_EXTRACT_LOG_MAX .
.TP
.B QBT_EXTRACT_SETTLE_TIMEOUT
Seconds to wait for unstable or missing content. Default: 15.
.TP
.B QBT_EXTRACT_LOCK_TIMEOUT
Seconds to wait for the shared lock. Default: 1800.
.TP
.B QBT_EXTRACT_LOG_MAX
Log size in bytes before rotation. Default: 1048576.
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Directory for the lock file
.IR qbt-extract.lock .
Falls back to
.IR /tmp .
.SH EXAMPLES
Run by hand as qBittorrent would, for one torrent:
.IP
.EX
qbt-extract.sh \\
  /mnt/shared/img/Downloads \\
  "/mnt/shared/img/Downloads/maldo - 2B [AI Generated].zip" \\
  "maldo - 2B [AI Generated]" Image
.EE
.P
Check what would happen for a whole directory without touching it:
.IP
.EX
QBT_EXTRACT_PATH=/tmp/torrents qbt-extract.sh \-n \\
  /tmp/torrents /tmp/torrents/Some.Pack Some.Pack Image
.EE
.P
Follow what the hook has been doing:
.IP
.EX
tail \-f ~/.local/share/qbt-extract.log
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Extraction succeeded, or the torrent was intentionally skipped (wrong
category, wrong path, no archives, content missing).
.TP
.B 1
An archive failed to extract (it is kept), the extractor returned an error,
or the lock could not be acquired.
.TP
.B 2
Wrong number of arguments or an unknown option.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/qbt-extract.log
Activity log, including the full output of the extractor.
.SH NOTES
Because the archive is deleted after a successful extraction, a torrent that
is still seeding will be reported as \(dqmissing files\(dq by qBittorrent
afterwards. This is expected with the default delete behaviour.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR extract_archives (1),
.BR flock (1),
.BR qbittorrent (1)
